{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795301034,"nonce":"4hVOIVQAmwGRrxzV1S5aTT4kEwQ=","title":"A new player learns the controls in the first minute of a match","message":"**Today.** The controls are in \"How to Play\", which a new player may never open. The first match starts with no hint, so a player who does not know that the plane follows the mouse can crash or circle without a shot.\n\n**Outcome.** The first match of a visit shows short hints in the first seconds, one at a time, for the device in the hand: steer, fire, missile, and flare. Each hint leaves once the player did it, or after a few seconds. The hints never cover the centre of the view.\n\n**Done when.** A browser test sees the first hint in the first match, sees it leave after the action, and sees no hint in a second match.\n\nAgent: Claude Opus 5.5","files":null}]}